{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"649f1f909ba3910dd32610da0d8fe1a40136d1e61d7fea9a1f98426abfb8dc82","slug":"covid-quiet-time","location":"/articles/covid-quiet-time/covid-quiet-time.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"COVID-19 lockdown leads to seismic noise “quiet period”","description":"A new study by an international team of scientists found lockdown measures to stop the spread of COVID-19 led to a 50 per cent reduction in seismic noise around the world. The researchers, including Meghan Miller and Louis Moresi from ANU analysed datasets from over 300 seismic stations.","banner":"/underworldcode.org-preview/9fee045526/build/banner-6391673a14a2d81e9f447ae669e865ec.png","keywords":["Geophysics","Python/Jupyter"],"parts":{"abstract":{"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","data":{"part":"abstract"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new study by an international team of scientists found lockdown measures to stop the spread of COVID-19 led to a 50 per cent reduction in seismic noise around the world. The researchers, including Meghan Miller and Louis Moresi from ANU analysed datasets from over 300 seismic stations.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"B8wfwXqICd"}],"key":"ijrgQPlmm6"}],"key":"tC6pwjyTdJ"}],"key":"KRvOYh6ASM"},"frontmatter":{"title":"COVID-19 lockdown leads to seismic noise “quiet period”","description":"A new study by an international team of scientists found lockdown measures to stop the spread of COVID-19 led to a 50 per cent reduction in seismic noise around the world. The researchers, including Meghan Miller and Louis Moresi from ANU analysed datasets from over 300 seismic stations.","banner":"/banner-6391673a14a2d81e9f447ae669e865ec.png","keywords":["Geophysics","Python/Jupyter"],"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Louis Moresi","given":"Louis","family":"Moresi"},"name":"